{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 12, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**Cherry Blossoms and City Lights: My Japan Adventure**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living postcard. The first morning, I wandered through the bustling Shibuya Crossing, watching a sea of umbrellas sway under neon signs. A quick bite of takoyaki from a street stall gave me the perfect fuel to dive into the city’s rhythm.\n\nThe next day, I escaped the urban buzz for the tranquil Meiji Shrine, where towering cedars framed a path of quiet reverence. Afterward, I hopped on the JR Yamanote line to Harajuku, losing myself in quirky boutiques and the sweet scent of crepes wafting from Takeshita Street.\n\nA bullet train whisked me west to Kyoto, where ancient temples greeted me with moss‑covered stone lanterns. I spent an afternoon at Kinkaku‑ji, the Golden Pavilion, its reflection shimmering on the pond like a mirage. Strolling through Gion, I caught a glimpse of a geisha hurrying to her evening appointment, her silk kimono a flash of elegance against the wooden machiya houses.\n\nNo trip to Japan is complete without a taste of its cuisine. I slurped steaming bowls of ramen in a tiny alleyway shop, savored melt‑in‑your‑mouth sushi at Tsukiji’s outer market, and ended each night with a warm mug of matcha while watching the city lights flicker below.\n\nFrom the neon‑lit streets of Tokyo to the serene gardens of Kyoto, Japan offered a perfect blend of tradition and modernity. Every moment felt like a new chapter, and I left with a suitcase full of memories—and a promise to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.18878544867038727}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.0025264269206672907}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.051180414855480194}, {"token": " write", "logprob": -0.6140906810760498}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.018306231126189232}, {"token": " short", "logprob": -0.00013136000779923052}, {"token": " blog", "logpro